---
/* eslint-disable astro/no-unused-css-selector */
---

<details class='group grid-col-1 grid gap-4'>
	<summary
		class='body-xs text-primary-100 border-secondary-100/30 bg-primary-20/30 order-2 col-start-1 w-fit cursor-pointer list-none rounded-xl border px-3 py-2 leading-6 transition-all duration-300 [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden'
	>
		<span class='overflow-visible group-open:hidden'>Read More</span>
		<span class='hidden overflow-visible group-open:inline'>Show Less</span>
	</summary>

	<div
		class='body-xs text-primary-80 col-start-0 grid gap-4 overflow-hidden leading-relaxed font-normal'
	>
		<p class='body-xs text-primary-80 leading-relaxed font-normal'>
			Currently, I&apos;m a <span class='text-primary-100 font-bold'>
				Senior Front-End Engineer
			</span> at
			<span class='text-primary-100 font-bold'>TelevisaUnivision</span>,
			specializing in performance and new features. I contribute to the creation
			and integration of UI components that power TelevisaUnivision&apos;s
			frontend, ensuring that the platform meets the highest standards of
			quality, performance, and best practices to deliver an outstanding user
			experience.
		</p>
		<p>
			In the past, I&apos;ve had the opportunity to develop software across a
			variety of environments, from <span class='text-primary-100 font-bold'>
				start-ups
			</span> to <span class='text-primary-100 font-bold'>
				large corporations
			</span> and <span class='text-primary-100 font-bold'>
				digital banking products
			</span>.
		</p>
	</div>
</details>

<style>
	details {
		overflow: clip;
	}

	details::details-content {
		display: grid;
		content-visibility: hidden;
		grid-template-rows: 0fr;
		transition:
			grid-template-rows 0.2s ease-out,
			content-visibility 0.2s allow-discrete;
	}

	details[open]::details-content {
		content-visibility: visible;
		grid-template-rows: 1fr;
	}

	@starting-style {
		details[open]::details-content {
			grid-template-rows: 0fr;
		}
	}
</style>
